1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[English subtitles are available]

2
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:09,810
[A Sikawasay or medium]

3
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:13,850
[refers to someone
blessed with the power of the gods.]

4
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:17,420
[They're spirit bearers]

5
00:00:17,990 --> 00:00:22,790
[and are humans' connection to the gods.]

6
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:27,230
[By the guidance of the gods,]

7
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:30,530
[Sikawasay help the people who are lost]

8
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:34,050
[find the right way to the gods.]

9
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:39,990
[They became mediums]

10
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:42,940
[not because they chose to do so.]

11
00:00:43,030 --> 00:00:46,370
[Almost all the mediums]

12
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:49,410
[experienced a life-threatening illness
when they were young.]

13
00:00:50,290 --> 00:00:52,570
[Only when a spirit]

14
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:56,970
[is willing to become
their guardian angel]

15
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:59,830
[can they get better.]

16
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:03,130
[In return,]

17
00:01:03,620 --> 00:01:07,270
[their future path will be the one]

18
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:13,430
[that God has walked on previously.]

19
00:01:20,910 --> 00:01:22,539
[By His arrangement,]

20
00:01:23,420 --> 00:01:26,539
[I came to the human world
bearing these gifts.]

21
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:28,960
[Oftentimes,]

22
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:32,520
[people have furrowed their eyebrows]

23
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,500
[because of this blessing.]

24
00:01:48,190 --> 00:01:49,020
[Sometimes,]

25
00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:53,420
[some people have to rest because of it.]

26
00:01:59,190 --> 00:02:01,830
I hate it when it rains.

27
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:05,430
The hairstyle I worked so hard on
is going to be ruined.

28
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:07,720
No.

29
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,240
I think the rain is nice.

30
00:02:11,330 --> 00:02:14,980
It's not good. Your shoes will get wet.

31
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:18,770
Are you stupid? Can't you wear sandals?

32
00:02:25,810 --> 00:02:26,730
The rain seems to have stopped.

33
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:27,790
It's true.

34
00:02:28,579 --> 00:02:30,560
Then I guess I can go on a date today.

35
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:36,980
[Only a few would remember or worry]

36
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:39,090
[about the momentary blessing.]

37
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:44,550
Hsieh Tien-ti.

38
00:02:45,470 --> 00:02:47,850
What are you doing? Come on.

39
00:02:49,079 --> 00:02:51,020
[Under the same rain,]

40
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:55,110
[every person has to go down]

41
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:57,040
[their own path that He has prepared.]

42
00:03:12,710 --> 00:03:16,230
[Episode 3, God Doesn't Roll the Dice]

43
00:04:47,570 --> 00:04:49,150
So why haven't you been able to find out

44
00:04:49,290 --> 00:04:51,440
why she is still unconscious?

45
00:04:51,530 --> 00:04:53,420
Ms. Chen, we ran a lot of tests,

46
00:04:53,510 --> 00:04:55,930
but we couldn't find out why.

47
00:04:56,060 --> 00:04:58,000
But based on her past medical history,

48
00:04:58,130 --> 00:05:00,720
this isn't the first time it happened.

49
00:05:00,810 --> 00:05:03,010
The same thing had happened to Ms. Hsieh.

50
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:05,390
We didn't know
why her fever wouldn't go down.

51
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:06,880
She also fell into unconsciousness.

52
00:05:06,970 --> 00:05:08,950
She stayed at our hospital
for a long time.

53
00:05:21,270 --> 00:05:24,700
[Grandma, what's a Sikawasay?]

54
00:05:25,540 --> 00:05:29,410
It's a person who can hear
and see spirits.

55
00:05:29,810 --> 00:05:31,790
Is that the same as you, Grandma?

56
00:05:32,450 --> 00:05:33,020
That's right.

57
00:05:33,990 --> 00:05:36,230
I want to become a Sikawasay too then.

58
00:05:37,460 --> 00:05:39,310
You want to be a Sikawasay?

59
00:05:41,030 --> 00:05:44,280
There are a lot of rules
you have to follow.

60
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:46,000
Like what?

61
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:47,850
For example,

62
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:53,300
you can't just do whatever you want.

63
00:05:55,330 --> 00:05:58,320
And you can't do what you want to do.

64
00:05:59,020 --> 00:06:00,120
You can't say no

65
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:02,760
to anyone who asks you for help.

66
00:06:12,710 --> 00:06:15,300
After you receive the gift of the Kawas,

67
00:06:16,750 --> 00:06:18,510
you'll be a Sikawasay.

68
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:24,370
You must turn yourself in to the Kawas.

69
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:27,890
Whether or not you can be a Sikawasay

70
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:32,290
is up to their will.

71
00:06:36,070 --> 00:06:37,650
Before I became a Sikawasay,

72
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:40,650
I was very sick one time.

73
00:06:40,730 --> 00:06:42,270
Sick?

74
00:06:42,409 --> 00:06:45,400
None of the doctors could treat me.

75
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:47,330
After that,

76
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:49,840
because a Kawas became my guardian angel,

77
00:06:49,970 --> 00:06:51,560
I finally recovered.

78
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:55,820
So you can't say no
to the Kawas' requests.

79
00:06:55,909 --> 00:06:57,409
You have to keep working

80
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,520
for them nonstop.

81
00:07:00,140 --> 00:07:01,460
The point is

82
00:07:02,910 --> 00:07:04,450
you can't leave the tribe.

83
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:06,870
Why is the Kawas so stingy?

84
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:09,020
That's too bad for you, Grandma.

85
00:07:09,290 --> 00:07:10,780
What do you know, brat?

86
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,540
Your grandma got better because of me.

87
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:18,310
That's right. Don't you feel bad for me?

88
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:20,290
So do you still want to be a Sikawasay?

89
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:23,280
I'll take over the role for you.

90
00:07:29,570 --> 00:07:31,240
Blessed it be.

91
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:33,840
Thank you, Banai.

92
00:07:34,190 --> 00:07:35,159
Thank you.

93
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:55,310
Tien-ti.

94
00:07:56,409 --> 00:07:57,250
Tien-ti!

95
00:07:59,710 --> 00:08:02,220
Tien-ti!

96
00:08:10,930 --> 00:08:11,810
Tien-ti!

97
00:08:13,830 --> 00:08:15,990
Tien-ti.

98
00:08:16,430 --> 00:08:18,230
Tien-ti, wake up. Come on.

99
00:08:18,370 --> 00:08:19,290
Tien-ti!

100
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:23,030
Give it up. She's mine now.

101
00:08:56,910 --> 00:08:59,590
[Give it up.]

102
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:03,990
[She's mine now.]

103
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:15,740
Cariwciw.

104
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:20,140
'Orad.

105
00:09:22,210 --> 00:09:23,040
'Orad?

106
00:09:25,460 --> 00:09:27,050
He's Kakarayan's messenger.

107
00:09:27,710 --> 00:09:29,030
This can't be good.

108
00:09:30,170 --> 00:09:31,540
Why are you here?

109
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:32,810
Those red eyes...

110
00:09:32,900 --> 00:09:34,530
The Kariah with the red eyes

111
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:36,330
isn't just any evil spirit.

112
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:40,950
You won't be able to save her.

113
00:09:43,370 --> 00:09:44,510
CPR!

114
00:09:46,230 --> 00:09:48,960
Tien-ti!

115
00:09:51,290 --> 00:09:52,300
Tien-ti!

116
00:10:25,830 --> 00:10:28,160
Wake up. It's me.

117
00:10:28,290 --> 00:10:29,530
Get up!

118
00:10:29,660 --> 00:10:31,070
Tien-ti!

119
00:10:31,770 --> 00:10:33,270
Tien-ti!

120
00:10:37,750 --> 00:10:38,810
Tien-ti.

121
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:51,960
Say it.

122
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:03,450
Just say what you're thinking.

123
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:12,200
Tell me what you want me to do for you.

124
00:11:12,290 --> 00:11:13,260
Let me save you.

125
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:16,650
Say it.

126
00:11:20,210 --> 00:11:21,530
Say it!

127
00:11:22,190 --> 00:11:24,080
Say it so I can save you.

128
00:11:25,180 --> 00:11:25,930
Say it.

129
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:30,990
Help me. I don't want to die.

130
00:11:31,210 --> 00:11:32,180
Louder.

131
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:35,000
Help me. I don't want to die!

132
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:36,980
Speak louder!

133
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:40,490
Help me! I don't want to die.

134
00:12:07,910 --> 00:12:09,270
My name is 'Orad.

135
00:12:10,810 --> 00:12:12,350
From now on,

136
00:12:13,410 --> 00:12:15,340
I will be your guardian angel.

137
00:14:01,690 --> 00:14:02,350
Aunt Su-chen.

138
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:08,950
You're awake.

139
00:14:10,310 --> 00:14:11,940
Why are we here?

140
00:14:12,030 --> 00:14:13,350
You fainted.

141
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:15,990
Yi-han called the ambulance

142
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:17,130
and brought you here.

143
00:14:17,260 --> 00:14:18,490
She called me too.

144
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:20,960
I rushed all the way here from Taipei.

145
00:14:21,090 --> 00:14:23,110
I was scared to death.

146
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:25,270
Thank God you're okay.

147
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:29,230
Why did you faint?

148
00:14:29,670 --> 00:14:31,250
Did something happen to you?

149
00:14:35,300 --> 00:14:36,710
I think...

150
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:45,330
We were eating at a restaurant
with the tour participants.

151
00:14:45,820 --> 00:14:47,000
[Then...]

152
00:14:48,410 --> 00:14:51,050
[I had to make a call.]

153
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:53,210
Grandma!

154
00:15:05,090 --> 00:15:07,160
I don't remember anything after that.

155
00:15:09,310 --> 00:15:10,500
How could this happen?

156
00:15:11,730 --> 00:15:14,110
When you were being examined,

157
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:16,750
they didn't find any signs of illness.

158
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:19,520
Or did you experience something triggering

159
00:15:19,610 --> 00:15:20,970
before you fainted?

160
00:15:34,430 --> 00:15:38,040
I don't remember, Aunt Su-chen.

161
00:15:40,070 --> 00:15:42,570
Okay, stop thinking about it.
Get some rest.

162
00:15:42,710 --> 00:15:44,550
You should lie down and rest.

163
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:45,650
I'll get the doctor.

164
00:16:24,420 --> 00:16:26,620
It's 36.5 degrees Celsius. It's normal.

165
00:16:26,750 --> 00:16:28,990
Miss, my fever has gone down.

166
00:16:29,130 --> 00:16:30,220
Can I go home?

167
00:16:30,310 --> 00:16:32,290
I want to go home with my grandma.

168
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:34,980
I'll have to ask the doctor.

169
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:37,700
The doctor will discuss it
with your grandma, okay?

170
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:46,330
Banai.

171
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:49,060
Are you really going to listen
to the messenger

172
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:51,080
and send Tien-ti away from here?

173
00:16:52,050 --> 00:16:53,630
If she doesn't leave,

174
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:56,490
she'll have to become a Sikawasay.

175
00:16:57,110 --> 00:16:59,480
That means the Kariah
will have the chance to hurt her.

176
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:04,760
This is the only thing I can do for her.

177
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:08,109
She's your only family.

178
00:17:08,770 --> 00:17:10,220
If she leaves,

179
00:17:10,660 --> 00:17:12,069
you'll surely regret it later.

180
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:13,079
Regret?

181
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:17,700
I've been a Sikawasay all my life.

182
00:17:17,790 --> 00:17:19,810
I don't have the right to regret it.

183
00:17:24,869 --> 00:17:26,849
I know the price I have to pay

184
00:17:28,830 --> 00:17:30,720
and the consequences of being a Sikawasay.

185
00:17:40,090 --> 00:17:43,260
She's still so young.

186
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:47,130
Her life has just begun.

187
00:17:55,580 --> 00:17:57,780
I can't let her live like me.

188
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:05,970
Unable to choose anything for herself

189
00:18:07,990 --> 00:18:12,650
and never being able to follow her heart.

190
00:18:57,400 --> 00:18:58,850
Take her away.

191
00:19:02,370 --> 00:19:05,410
Place her in a world without Kawas.

192
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:11,520
Don't let her know she's a Sikawasay.

193
00:19:13,990 --> 00:19:15,480
Don't look for me.

194
00:19:18,170 --> 00:19:19,710
Don't ever come back.

195
00:19:25,870 --> 00:19:27,540
Don't worry about that.

196
00:19:28,550 --> 00:19:31,410
I won't let her become a Sikawasay.

197
00:19:32,770 --> 00:19:35,280
I won't let the Kariah harm her either.

198
00:19:37,040 --> 00:19:37,970
That is the reason

199
00:19:38,050 --> 00:19:39,950
Kakarayan sent me here.

200
00:20:39,300 --> 00:20:43,000
[Treatment schedule]

201
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:41,060
So can she eat seafood

202
00:20:41,150 --> 00:20:45,150
-like shrimp and squid?
-Make sure she stays away from those.

203
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:46,960
She can't eat those things?

204
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:48,630
She can't eat a lot of things.

205
00:20:48,720 --> 00:20:50,650
Then...

206
00:20:50,740 --> 00:20:52,410
-So I'll keep to...
-Aunt Su-chen.

207
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:56,720
How are you feeling? Are you okay?

208
00:20:56,810 --> 00:20:57,910
I'm better now.

209
00:20:59,190 --> 00:21:00,550
Let's go back to Taipei together.

210
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:02,440
Back to Taipei?

211
00:21:04,420 --> 00:21:06,670
I asked my brother to book a doctor.

212
00:21:06,800 --> 00:21:08,120
He was a teacher at a medical school.

213
00:21:08,210 --> 00:21:10,280
He's a very famous cardiologist.

214
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:11,290
He has outpatient consultation tomorrow.

215
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:12,520
We can go to see him.

216
00:21:13,930 --> 00:21:15,510
But...

217
00:21:15,640 --> 00:21:17,360
I can't go back to Taipei yet.

218
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:19,910
You can't go back to Taipei?

219
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:22,290
Your health is more important now.

220
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:25,370
I know the doctor here
didn't find anything.

221
00:21:25,450 --> 00:21:26,420
But you were unconscious for so long.

222
00:21:26,510 --> 00:21:28,090
This isn't the first time.

223
00:21:28,230 --> 00:21:29,550
You were admitted to the hospital
when you were little too.

224
00:21:29,630 --> 00:21:31,000
Do you remember?

225
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:35,090
Tien-ti!

226
00:21:48,600 --> 00:21:52,250
[Does the fainting
have something to do with him?]

227
00:21:55,370 --> 00:21:57,270
Aunt Su-chen, I have something to do.

228
00:21:58,230 --> 00:21:59,510
I'll go back to Taipei in a few days.

229
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:01,140
Tell me where the doctor is.

230
00:22:01,230 --> 00:22:02,500
I'll make sure to see him.

231
00:22:02,590 --> 00:22:04,530
Don't wait for me. Go home first.

232
00:22:04,750 --> 00:22:05,580
Tien-ti.

233
00:22:25,600 --> 00:22:26,390
Are you angry?

234
00:22:27,490 --> 00:22:28,940
Is it because I was picking on you

235
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:30,350
or because I hurt her?

236
00:22:35,590 --> 00:22:37,350
Don't be mad.

237
00:22:37,440 --> 00:22:38,930
The result is the same anyway.

238
00:22:39,020 --> 00:22:40,560
Whether she dies
by Kakarayan's arrangement

239
00:22:40,690 --> 00:22:42,360
or by my hands,

240
00:22:43,330 --> 00:22:44,120
what's the difference?

241
00:23:50,470 --> 00:23:51,400
What are you doing here?

242
00:23:52,760 --> 00:23:53,470
Grandma.

243
00:23:58,000 --> 00:23:58,700
I told you.

244
00:23:58,830 --> 00:24:00,860
This isn't your home anymore.

245
00:24:00,950 --> 00:24:01,960
What are you doing here?

246
00:24:04,250 --> 00:24:04,770
Go back!

247
00:24:07,940 --> 00:24:08,820
Grandma.

248
00:24:08,950 --> 00:24:09,970
Grandma, I'll go.

249
00:24:10,540 --> 00:24:11,200
But before I go,

250
00:24:11,290 --> 00:24:13,090
can you do me one last favor?

251
00:24:13,220 --> 00:24:14,630
I have nothing to do with you.

252
00:24:15,550 --> 00:24:16,520
Why should I oblige?

253
00:24:17,710 --> 00:24:18,980
Can you tell me

254
00:24:19,510 --> 00:24:21,670
how I can become a Sikawasay?

255
00:24:32,490 --> 00:24:34,470
Sikawasay?

256
00:24:43,980 --> 00:24:46,570
You said you want to become a Sikawasay?

257
00:24:50,620 --> 00:24:53,000
I want to become a Sikawasay
just like you.

258
00:24:53,130 --> 00:24:54,980
Do you have any idea what it takes?

259
00:24:55,060 --> 00:24:55,500
I know.

260
00:24:55,590 --> 00:24:56,910
Then why are you doing this?

261
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:58,760
Grandma, have you forgotten?

262
00:24:59,820 --> 00:25:01,400
You told me when I was a kid

263
00:25:01,530 --> 00:25:03,780
whether or not we can become a Sikawasay

264
00:25:03,910 --> 00:25:06,020
is not up to us.

265
00:25:38,890 --> 00:25:39,770
I don't understand.

266
00:25:40,780 --> 00:25:41,610
Now, you want to teach Tien-ti

267
00:25:41,700 --> 00:25:43,370
how to become a Sikawasay?

268
00:25:43,990 --> 00:25:45,750
Haven't you always blamed me

269
00:25:45,880 --> 00:25:48,130
for choosing you to become one?

270
00:25:50,550 --> 00:25:52,220
You always do this when you're in denial.

271
00:25:52,390 --> 00:25:53,540
You won't even answer me.

272
00:25:54,860 --> 00:25:56,270
I'm leaving this place soon.

273
00:25:59,350 --> 00:26:00,050
Forget it.

274
00:26:00,890 --> 00:26:01,460
You're not going to listen

275
00:26:01,590 --> 00:26:02,780
to a word I say anyway.

276
00:26:21,210 --> 00:26:21,780
Banai.

277
00:26:22,930 --> 00:26:24,420
Are you thinking

278
00:26:25,260 --> 00:26:26,490
that you should have never sent Tien-ti

279
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:29,920
to Taipei in the beginning?

280
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:34,020
Because of your own regrets,

281
00:26:34,850 --> 00:26:36,610
you made the decision for her.

282
00:26:42,950 --> 00:26:45,410
You did the best you could, Banai.

283
00:26:48,360 --> 00:26:49,680
In this world,

284
00:26:51,310 --> 00:26:52,500
other than Kakarayan,

285
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:56,680
no one knows for sure
if a decision is the right one.

286
00:26:59,930 --> 00:27:02,750
[The first step to becoming a Sikawasay]

287
00:27:03,280 --> 00:27:04,820
[is to make yourself]

288
00:27:04,900 --> 00:27:07,100
[a vessel for the spirit.]

289
00:27:07,760 --> 00:27:09,960
[That's also the hardest step.]

290
00:27:10,670 --> 00:27:12,160
[So at this point,]

291
00:27:12,650 --> 00:27:15,730
[with the help of alcohol,]

292
00:27:16,870 --> 00:27:18,670
[we'll forget about our own existence]

293
00:27:19,640 --> 00:27:23,510
[and give ourselves entirely to God.]

294
00:27:31,650 --> 00:27:33,990
Don't tell me you think
you'll be able to change the end

295
00:27:34,510 --> 00:27:35,830
by becoming a Sikawasay.

296
00:27:36,490 --> 00:27:37,240
Won't it?

297
00:27:38,610 --> 00:27:40,410
Then why are you here right now?

298
00:27:40,810 --> 00:27:41,550
And why did I recall

299
00:27:41,640 --> 00:27:43,750
everything about you?

300
00:27:43,840 --> 00:27:45,560
Why is it that after you appeared,

301
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:49,120
I've started having
those strange symptoms again?

302
00:27:49,210 --> 00:27:50,930
You don't have to worry
about that anymore.

303
00:27:51,540 --> 00:27:52,730
Your friends' memories

304
00:27:52,820 --> 00:27:54,310
have all been sorted.

305
00:27:54,450 --> 00:27:57,000
From now on, you'll forget everything.

306
00:27:59,950 --> 00:28:02,230
Stop combing my hair!

307
00:28:02,320 --> 00:28:04,210
Why do I have to die?

308
00:28:04,300 --> 00:28:06,590
You've been my guardian angel
all these years.

309
00:28:06,680 --> 00:28:08,570
You must know that I'm ordinary.

310
00:28:08,660 --> 00:28:10,500
I couldn't be more ordinary.

311
00:28:10,590 --> 00:28:11,960
The world will continue to operate

312
00:28:12,040 --> 00:28:13,580
with or without me.

313
00:28:13,670 --> 00:28:15,740
Why can't you just leave me alone?

314
00:28:18,600 --> 00:28:20,180
That's not for me to decide.

315
00:28:20,270 --> 00:28:21,370
You can!

316
00:28:21,500 --> 00:28:23,750
I'm sure you can. You're a god.

317
00:28:23,840 --> 00:28:24,940
If you wish to save me,

318
00:28:25,070 --> 00:28:26,300
I'm sure you can do it.

319
00:28:26,430 --> 00:28:28,720
Even if I'm a god,
there are things I can't do.

320
00:28:37,080 --> 00:28:39,320
In this world, there is only one

321
00:28:40,820 --> 00:28:41,740
omnipotent god.

322
00:28:42,890 --> 00:28:44,030
That is Kakarayan.

323
00:28:45,480 --> 00:28:47,860
Your fate is in Kakarayan's
Reflection of Time.

324
00:28:48,700 --> 00:28:50,060
It has all been decided.

325
00:28:50,900 --> 00:28:51,860
What?

326
00:28:53,180 --> 00:28:53,980
Reflection?

327
00:28:56,220 --> 00:28:57,890
When I close my eyes,

328
00:28:57,980 --> 00:28:59,340
things of the future

329
00:28:59,920 --> 00:29:02,340
will play before me like reflections.

330
00:29:02,910 --> 00:29:03,880
These are all reflections

331
00:29:04,010 --> 00:29:05,500
that Kakarayan has arranged beforehand.

332
00:29:06,910 --> 00:29:08,490
As the messenger,

333
00:29:08,670 --> 00:29:10,340
I'm only carrying out

334
00:29:11,490 --> 00:29:13,070
the reflections one by one.

335
00:29:13,950 --> 00:29:15,620
From when I saved you as a kid

336
00:29:16,720 --> 00:29:18,220
to becoming your guardian angel

337
00:29:19,450 --> 00:29:20,590
and watching you die

338
00:29:21,830 --> 00:29:23,850
before the end of days,

339
00:29:27,500 --> 00:29:29,040
they are all prearranged.

340
00:29:31,110 --> 00:29:32,120
It can't be changed.

341
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:35,250
If it can't be changed,

342
00:29:37,140 --> 00:29:39,250
then when you saw the reflection,

343
00:29:40,610 --> 00:29:44,350
you shouldn't have appeared
at my house that day.

344
00:29:44,930 --> 00:29:46,030
Neither should I

345
00:29:46,250 --> 00:29:48,840
have seen my moment of death
in the future.

346
00:29:50,470 --> 00:29:53,070
And I broke that comb.

347
00:29:53,330 --> 00:29:55,490
No way. There has to be a way.

348
00:29:56,500 --> 00:29:58,700
At least you can choose from now on

349
00:29:58,920 --> 00:30:01,120
not to look at the darn reflection again.

350
00:30:02,570 --> 00:30:04,460
I'm begging you.

351
00:30:04,550 --> 00:30:05,780
I have so much more

352
00:30:05,870 --> 00:30:07,540
I want to do.

353
00:30:07,630 --> 00:30:08,990
I don't want to die yet.

354
00:30:09,080 --> 00:30:10,580
What if I let you know

355
00:30:10,710 --> 00:30:13,350
that the future you hope for
doesn't exist?

356
00:30:14,360 --> 00:30:15,500
What do you mean?

357
00:30:44,940 --> 00:30:46,130
This is...

358
00:30:47,450 --> 00:30:49,250
This is the Reflection of Time I saw.

359
00:30:50,620 --> 00:30:52,460
It's the future you've been hoping for.

360
00:30:54,750 --> 00:30:56,120
This is the future?

361
00:30:57,170 --> 00:30:57,740
Yes.

362
00:30:59,500 --> 00:31:01,400
This is the future of humanity.

363
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:05,400
The future without
the blessings of Kakarayan.

364
00:31:08,080 --> 00:31:10,460
When the last rainfall of the world comes,

365
00:31:12,570 --> 00:31:14,200
when Kakarayan takes away

366
00:31:14,950 --> 00:31:16,880
all the Kawas in the world,

367
00:31:17,670 --> 00:31:20,360
rain will never fall again.

368
00:31:20,840 --> 00:31:22,290
The waters will no longer flow.

369
00:31:23,040 --> 00:31:25,370
Time will no longer mean anything.

370
00:31:28,230 --> 00:31:29,250
Is such a future

371
00:31:29,860 --> 00:31:30,920
still something

372
00:31:31,090 --> 00:31:33,070
that you wish to live in?

373
00:31:44,120 --> 00:31:46,360
Hsieh Tien-ti, why are you awake?

374
00:31:46,580 --> 00:31:47,640
Why don't you rest more?

375
00:31:50,010 --> 00:31:51,200
Are you sick again?

376
00:31:54,940 --> 00:31:56,000
That's good.

377
00:31:56,310 --> 00:31:57,710
Thank God.

378
00:31:57,850 --> 00:31:59,740
I even got this amulet for you.

379
00:31:59,830 --> 00:32:00,490
Here.

380
00:31:59,960 --> 00:32:01,190
[Good luck amulet]

381
00:32:04,840 --> 00:32:05,900
I'm glad you're okay.

382
00:32:06,070 --> 00:32:07,000
If my mom finds out

383
00:32:07,130 --> 00:32:08,180
that something happened to you,

384
00:32:08,270 --> 00:32:09,940
I'll be dead.

385
00:32:10,030 --> 00:32:11,530
It's not your fault that I fell sick.

386
00:32:11,620 --> 00:32:13,420
Why would your mom blame you?

387
00:32:13,510 --> 00:32:16,060
Didn't we agree
that I'd be in charge this time?

388
00:32:16,150 --> 00:32:17,910
I was afraid of trouble.

389
00:32:18,040 --> 00:32:19,890
That's why I got you to Taitung.

390
00:32:19,980 --> 00:32:21,600
I reckoned if something happened,

391
00:32:21,690 --> 00:32:23,670
at least you could help me out.

392
00:32:24,160 --> 00:32:25,780
Otherwise,
you wouldn't have been dragged here.

393
00:32:26,310 --> 00:32:27,100
You mean

394
00:32:28,470 --> 00:32:30,620
you asked for me to come?

395
00:32:31,110 --> 00:32:31,900
Yes.

396
00:32:32,300 --> 00:32:34,360
I persuaded my mom for such a long time.

397
00:32:34,580 --> 00:32:35,640
I even promised her

398
00:32:35,730 --> 00:32:38,150
that I wouldn't leave everything to you.

399
00:32:38,240 --> 00:32:38,680
That's why she said okay.

400
00:32:38,760 --> 00:32:40,610
[You don't have to worry
about that anymore.]

401
00:32:40,700 --> 00:32:41,580
Your friends' memories

402
00:32:41,670 --> 00:32:43,340
have all been sorted.

403
00:32:44,310 --> 00:32:47,040
From now on, you'll forget everything.

404
00:32:50,200 --> 00:32:51,700
I'm glad you're okay.

405
00:32:57,160 --> 00:32:58,740
Guys.

406
00:32:58,830 --> 00:33:00,720
You guys are delicious.

407
00:33:00,850 --> 00:33:01,990
Delicious?

408
00:33:02,080 --> 00:33:03,090
No.

409
00:33:03,180 --> 00:33:04,850
I mean, you guys are handsome.

410
00:33:04,940 --> 00:33:06,880
Thank you.

411
00:33:06,970 --> 00:33:07,710
You there.

412
00:33:08,810 --> 00:33:09,910
What's your type?

413
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:10,790
I'm AB.

414
00:33:11,190 --> 00:33:11,980
No.

415
00:33:12,070 --> 00:33:12,860
What is it then?

416
00:33:13,570 --> 00:33:15,020
You're my ideal type.

417
00:33:20,610 --> 00:33:23,330
[Rain will never fall again.]

418
00:33:24,080 --> 00:33:25,710
[The waters will no longer flow.]

419
00:33:27,030 --> 00:33:30,460
[Time will no longer mean anything.]

420
00:33:31,390 --> 00:33:32,710
[Is such a future]

421
00:33:33,100 --> 00:33:34,330
[still something]

422
00:33:34,420 --> 00:33:35,960
[that you wish to live in?]

423
00:33:44,010 --> 00:33:45,290
[You showed me this]

424
00:33:45,380 --> 00:33:46,260
[because you want me]

425
00:33:46,390 --> 00:33:48,550
[to lose the will
to continue living, right?]

426
00:33:53,030 --> 00:33:55,010
I'm just an ordinary person.

427
00:33:55,890 --> 00:33:57,870
You think too highly of me.

428
00:33:57,960 --> 00:34:00,380
I'm not trying to change the world.

429
00:34:01,480 --> 00:34:02,980
I told you.

430
00:34:03,060 --> 00:34:04,340
My existence in this world

431
00:34:04,430 --> 00:34:06,890
doesn't matter.

432
00:34:06,980 --> 00:34:08,920
The only thing I can change

433
00:34:09,050 --> 00:34:10,370
and the only thing I want to change

434
00:34:10,460 --> 00:34:12,080
is to live my simple life

435
00:34:12,219 --> 00:34:13,710
a little bit better.

436
00:34:13,800 --> 00:34:15,909
That's all I want.

437
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:17,100
As for something

438
00:34:17,190 --> 00:34:19,300
that will happen
a few hundred years later,

439
00:34:19,389 --> 00:34:21,940
I don't think I'm able to change anything.

440
00:34:22,030 --> 00:34:23,830
So it has nothing to do with me.

441
00:34:23,920 --> 00:34:24,800
You're wrong.

442
00:34:26,210 --> 00:34:28,409
This is not a world
that's far into the future.

443
00:34:48,429 --> 00:34:51,110
[2025, Unrest in many European countries
due to dispute over water sources]

444
00:34:51,770 --> 00:34:52,480
["The Global Times"]

445
00:34:57,620 --> 00:34:58,460
[Do you still think]

446
00:34:58,550 --> 00:35:00,260
[it has nothing to do with you?]

447
00:35:14,390 --> 00:35:25,390
[Great fortune and luck]

448
00:35:47,830 --> 00:35:48,930
[I don't understand.]

449
00:35:49,850 --> 00:35:51,870
[You said you're able to see the future.]

450
00:35:52,840 --> 00:35:54,420
So what you're showing me now

451
00:35:54,510 --> 00:35:55,660
is part of the future?

452
00:35:59,480 --> 00:36:00,630
So since the moment

453
00:36:00,760 --> 00:36:02,920
you became my guardian angel,

454
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:05,510
you've known what would happen?

455
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:08,680
In that case,

456
00:36:09,740 --> 00:36:11,500
why did you protect me?
